# Raw source data: 1GB+, individual files up to 119.6MB (exceeds GitHub's
# 100MB per-file limit). Not a "result" -- regenerable via step1-step3d,
# documented in RUNBOOK.md. Excluded from the freeze commit deliberately;
# remove this line if you want it version-controlled anyway.
data/

# Python bytecode cache -- never meaningful to version.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local virtual environment -- requirements.txt is the source of truth for
# reproducing it, not the folder itself.
.venv/

# LaTeX build artifacts (report.pdf itself is NOT excluded, only intermediates)
pdf_report/*.aux
pdf_report/*.log
pdf_report/*.out
pdf_report/*.toc

# Old restore-point archive from a folder reorganisation, incl. a 124.9MB
# OSM/Overpass API response cache backup. Kept on local disk on purpose
# (re-downloading OSM data is slow) but this is a code+data repo, not a
# backup service -- doesn't belong in the public GitHub history.
05_archive_deleted_20260716_0701/

# The dissertation manuscript is authored and submitted elsewhere (see
# WRITING_HANDOFF_v6.md's separate writing workflow); this repo is the
# code/data/results side only. dissertation.tex and pdf_report/report.tex
# are both superseded/stale relative to the actual current draft, so
# publishing them here would mislead anyone who finds this repo.
# (dissertation_colab.ipynb stays IN the repo -- it's a runnable pipeline
# mirror, i.e. code, not manuscript text.)
dissertation.tex
pdf_report/
Dissertation_Technical_Report.pdf
data_and_software_availability_FILLED.tex

# Comparison against supervisor feedback -- not for public upload.
supervisor_comparison_results.xlsx
# 5-fold smoke-test byproducts (--quick flag) -- zero scientific value, no
# number anywhere is cited from one of these. The real, full result each
# is a smoke test *for* stays tracked.
*_quick.csv

# Consolidated into supplementary_experiments.ipynb (same code, one file
# instead of six loose scripts). Kept on local disk, not tracked.
scan_sl_routes.py
step4k_rf_feature_importance.py
step4l_multiseed_mlp.py
step4m_alt_target_activity.py
step4n_gatv2_edge_attrs.py
step4o_tabular_ensemble.py

# Figures (*.png, *.pdf) are cheap to regenerate -- seconds to minutes,
# from step8_dissertation_figures.py / step8b*.py against the result CSVs
# already tracked below. The CSVs themselves stay tracked: each one is the
# output of a 33-fold CV run that took 1.5-2h of CPU time, and isn't
# regenerable without redoing that compute. (fig5_fold_structure.pdf is a
# figure like the rest, matched by the *.pdf rule -- not excluded specially.)
*.png
*.pdf